es be  able to gather again at christmas i  think that's extremely important  i would love to do so with my own family  but the way to get there  is for us all to abide by the basic  rules  today and for the work of the government  and local leaders to progress swiftly  so that in those places where the virus  is concentrated we take decisive action  now and give the country the best  possible chance of being in a good  position  for christmas okay so the police have to  do what the police have to do more than  a million people have signed  the marcus rashford petition for uh free  school  meals for kids when they're not at  school  is there any point in me asking you  whether you might change that for  christmas  well we've said that we'll continue to  uh keep that  under review we all share the same  objective  of course we want to ensure that young  people and children get  the best possible life chances that's at  the absolute heart  of the moral mission of this government  of the conservative party  we're doing that in a number of  different ways recently  we gave 63 million pounds to local  councils so that they can help to  support children and vulnerable people  through the autumn that money is is  coming towards the end of  uh the period in which it was due to be  spent if we need to take further action  we will do there's no dispute on what is  our goal here  what is uh up for debate is the best way  to achieve it  and there there is a legitimate argument  about whether it's through  uh further advances in free school meals  whether it's through  targeted support of the kind that we've  been doing recently through local  councils  or it's through the benefit system where  also we've been putting extra money we  put nine billion pounds remember  additional funding into universal credit  and further support for local housing  allowance  to give families on the lowest incomes  in the country more money  in their pockets as they try to weather  a difficult yea